Usually we don't handle cancellation in our completable future wrappers (maybe we should?). I'm not sure this would actually be enough, might need to also override `newIncompleteFuture` to ensure cancellation propagates when stages are added to the returned completable future. In the only place we handle cancellation we use
```java
  @Override
  public boolean cancel(boolean mayInterruptIfRunning) {
    boolean result = super.cancel(mayInterruptIfRunning);
    future.cancel(mayInterruptIfRunning);
    return result;
  } 
